---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/therapy-billing-software/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">Mental health EHR</a>{" "}
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">Cash-Pay Therapy Billing &amp; Payments</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="ed-feature-hero">
        <section class="ed-hero">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Cash-pay billing for mental health</div>
            <h1>
              Finish the visit.
              <br />
              <em>Keep payment moving.</em>
            </h1>
            <p class="ed-dek">
              Otto carries the visit into cash-pay billing with a prefilled
              procedure code, fee review, and payment collection. Keep the
              payment step connected to the work you have already done.
            </p>
            <div class="ed-actions">
              <a class="button" href="/waitlist/">
                Join the waitlist ↗
              </a>
              <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
                Watch the 2-minute demo ↗
              </a>
            </div>
            <p class="micro">
              For independent mental health practices · Built by Tebra
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ed-hero-art">
            <div class="art">
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 640 500"
                preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect width="640" height="500" fill="#e0d3c8" />
                <path d="M0 0h250v500H0z" fill="#e8e5df" />
                <path d="M65 310V150a115 115 0 0 1 230 0v160" fill="#b3c6c4" />
                <circle cx="179" cy="156" r="59" fill="#f6f3eb" />
                <path
                  d="M179 43v265M64 167h230"
                  stroke="#f6f3eb"
                  stroke-width="3"
                />
                <path d="m0 385 640-130v245H0Z" fill="#8ca7a2" />
                <ellipse
                  cx="347"
                  cy="410"
                  rx="210"
                  ry="39"
                  fill="#004852"
                  opacity=".09"
                />
                <g transform="translate(280 90) rotate(10 110 150)">
                  <rect
                    x="9"
                    y="13"
                    width="216"
                    height="280"
                    rx="16"
                    fill="#004852"
                    opacity=".14"
                  />
                  <rect width="216" height="280" rx="15" fill="#f6f3eb" />
                  <rect
                    x="25"
                    y="28"
                    width="166"
                    height="67"
                    rx="9"
                    fill="#cbdde0"
                  />
                  <text
                    x="108"
                    y="75"
                    text-anchor="middle"
                    fill="#004852"
                    font-family="sans-serif"
                    font-size="35"
                  >
                    $173.61
                  </text>
                  <g fill="#e0d3c8">
                    <rect x="25" y="117" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="86" y="117" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="148" y="117" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="25" y="167" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="86" y="167" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="25" y="217" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                    <rect x="86" y="217" width="43" height="35" rx="7" />
                  </g>
                  <rect
                    x="148"
                    y="167"
                    width="43"
                    height="85"
                    rx="7"
                    fill="#b85c38"
                  />
                  <path
                    d="M160 201h19m-19 10h19"
                    stroke="#f6f3eb"
                    stroke-width="3"
                  />
                </g>
                <path d="M141 390v-85" stroke="#004852" stroke-width="3" />
                <path
                  d="M141 343c-55-2-55-44-55-44 47 1 55 44 55 44m0-18c48-2 55-48 55-48-45 0-55 48-55 48"
                  fill="#417e86"
                />
                <path d="M110 368h62l-10 49h-43z" fill="#f6f3eb" />
              </svg>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">The work, connected</span>
            <h2>From the encounter to a reviewed charge.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Clinical documentation and payment belong to the same visit. Review
            each step with the context of the encounter still close.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>Review the code</h3>
            <p>
              Check the suggested procedure code against the service and
              documentation. Use review and override when needed.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Confirm the charge</h3>
            <p>
              Review the fee schedule, charge details, and payment timing before
              collecting.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Keep track of payment</h3>
            <p>
              Otto lists Stripe Connect, receipts, refunds, payment links,
              billing history, and balance alerts.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-story">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Inside the workflow</span>
          <h2>A payment workflow for self-pay care.</h2>
          <p>
            Otto’s early experience centers on cash-pay practices. Use the
            connected workflow to move from signed documentation into the review
            of charges and collection.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/demo/#watch">
            See the complete visit ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <ul class="ed-checks">
          <li>Procedure-code prefill with review and override</li>
          <li>Fee schedules and flexible collection</li>
          <li>Payment links, receipts, and refunds</li>
          <li>Balances and billing history in the patient record</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Does a prefilled code guarantee correct billing?</summary>
            <p>
              No. You must verify that the code, service, duration,
              documentation, and fee are appropriate before finalizing the
              charge.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does Otto submit insurance claims?</summary>
            <p>
              Confirm current insurance support directly with the team before
              choosing Otto. This page describes cash-pay collection and does
              not promise claims submission, eligibility, or reimbursement.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is the free superbill generator part of the EHR?</summary>
            <p>
              The <a href="/tools/superbill/">free superbill generator</a> is a
              separate browser tool in this resource site. Its presence does not
              establish an integrated superbill workflow inside Otto.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What payment fees apply?</summary>
            <p>
              Confirm processing fees, subscription terms, and any usage charges
              before subscribing. The <a href="/waitlist/">Otto team</a> can
              answer questions about your practice.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</span>
        <div class="ed-resources">
          <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">The mental health EHR ↗</a>
          <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">AI progress notes ↗</a>
          <a href="/compare/">Compare your options ↗</a>
          <a href="/tools/">Free practice tools ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
      <p class="ed-source">
        Product details checked against{" "}
        <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto’s public website</a> on October
        16, 2026. Confirm availability and service terms for your practice.
        Workflow examples are illustrative and use fictional information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
